<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulster Unionist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1905–</span> · Also known as UUP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ulster Unionist Party is a unionist political party in Northern Ireland, founded in 1905 as the Ulster Unionist Council to oppose Irish home rule. It governed Northern Ireland without interruption from 1921 to 1972, under leaders such as James Craig and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terence">Terence</a> O'Neill. Its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Trimble helped negotiate the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> of 1998 and became the first First Minister, but the party was later overtaken by the Democratic Unionist Party.</p></div>
